From: QEMU Lightning OpenGL integration
Subject: [dependency configuration] Use Mesa's existing TLS qsort fallback on NT5

Module: qemu_lightning.opengl.reactos_mesa_capabilities
Purpose: Select the existing upstream sort fallback instead of an unavailable CRT export.
Created: 2026-10-21
Architecture: Meson capability input only; no authored renderer implementation.

Target: Mesa ed458ffac6f410e6f03e54d17f47e8aeb55fe3a1
ReactOS0.4.16 filters qsort_s from msvcrt's NT5 exports. A cross SDK link
check cannot establish the guest DLL's exports. Removing this detection uses
the existing util_tls_qsort_r implementation without new renderer code.
Mesa meson.build retains its upstream MIT license and copyright notices.

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1689,7 +1689,6 @@ functions_to_detect = {
   'flock': '',
   'strtok_r': '',
   'getrandom': '#include <sys/random.h>',
-  'qsort_s': '',
   'posix_fallocate': '',
   'secure_getenv': '',
   'sysconf': '#include <unistd.h>',
